          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>A 45-year-old man records a blood pressure of 136/84 mmHg. How is this reading c</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>A 45-year-old man records a blood pressure of 136/84 mmHg. How is this reading classified under the ACC/AHA 2017 guideline compared with the JNC 7 system?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Stage 1 hypertension under both systems</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Under JNC 7, hypertension begins at 140/90 mmHg. A reading of 136/84 falls in the pre-hypertension range (120–139 systolic or 80–89 diastolic), not Stage 1.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Stage 1 under ACC/AHA 2017; pre-hypertension under JNC 7</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>The ACC/AHA 2017 guideline sets hypertension at 130/80, making 136/84 Stage 1. Under JNC 7, hypertension starts at 140/90, so the same reading is only pre-hypertension.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Pre-hypertension under both systems</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Under ACC/AHA 2017, hypertension begins at 130/80 mmHg, so 136/84 already qualifies as Stage 1 — not pre-hypertension.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Normal under ACC/AHA 2017; Stage 1 under JNC 7</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>This reverses both classifications. The ACC/AHA 2017 uses the lower threshold (130/80) and therefore captures this reading as hypertensive, while JNC 7 (threshold 140/90) does not.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "Remember: ACC/AHA 2017 defines hypertension at ≥130/80 mmHg, while JNC 7 uses ≥140/90. The Indian Guidelines (IGH-IV) follow the JNC 7 threshold."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Well done. The same blood pressure reading can change category depending on which guideline you cite — always specify the system."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
